      "what": "The baseline documented that clients could paginate by specifying a `limit` parameter (returning up to 100 items). The candidate introduces a new requirement: use a `cursor` for pagination instead of relying solely on `limit`. It also reduces the maximum return size from 100 to 50.",
      "how": "Clients written against the baseline that send requests with only a `limit` parameter (e.g., `GET /pets?limit=20`) may no longer receive results or may encounter unexpected behavior if the server now strictly requires a `cursor`. The maximum batch size is also halved, requiring more requests to retrieve the same dataset.",
      "severity": "breaking",
      "baselineRef": "Returns up to `limit` pets (max 100)",
      "changeIds": ["md:Petstore API > Pets > List pets#1"]
    }
  ],"risks": [
