      "description": "Clients using only the `limit` parameter may fail to retrieve data if the server now enforces a `cursor` requirement.",
      "failureScenario": "A client sends `GET /pets?limit=50`. The baseline expected up to 50 items. The candidate implies pagination via `cursor`, suggesting the server might reject requests without it or return fewer/more items than expected if the cursor logic is different.","affectedConsumers": "Any client using `limit` for pagination without also implementing `cursor` support.","likelihood": "high","impact": "high","mitigation": "Update clients to support both `limit` (if backward compatible) or migrate to `cursor`-based pagination immediately. Verify the server's actual behavior regarding missing cursors."
